--- body ---
## Context
Author decision, 2026-11-01: rebuild the stack simple and efficient; drop R2R
and its companions. deploy/compose.yaml runs about 16 services: r2r and
r2r-dashboard, two Postgres (pgvector and Hatchet's), Hatchet (engine,
dashboard, migration, setup, RabbitMQ), MinIO, Unstructured,
graph_clustering, Nginx Proxy Manager, the monitor and the frontend. R2R is
wired into src/intake (push.py, cull.py, verify.py), src/frontend (direct
calls to /v3/retrieval/rag), the smoke tests, deploy/ops and pyproject.toml.

Direction already decided elsewhere: internal service on inari (0013, Podman,
no GPU, 71 GB RAM free), no personal data collection (0013), Albert for
embeddings, retrieval or generation (0009), reranker (0012), CIRED archives
read in place (0015), hardcopies catalogue (0014).

## Imagine first
One design note shared with 0009 (template: problem, situation, state of the
art, alternatives, synthesis with costs, phased plan, double advisor review +
KISS). Candidate shapes, simplest first:
- A. Albert end to end: Albert collections hold the chunks, Albert search and
  rerank retrieve, Albert generates; Cirdi is a static page plus a thin
  proxy that holds the key. Nothing stateful on inari.
- B. One small Python service (FastAPI or similar) with an embedded vector
  store in a single file (SQLite with a vector extension, LanceDB or
  DuckDB) on inari, Albert for embeddings, rerank and generation.
- C. B with one Postgres + pgvector, only if B's store falls short.
Judge on: services to run (target: one process plus Apache), lines of code,
latency, cost, how intake and re-ingestion work, and what the solo maintainer
must patch.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Design note accepted, with the chosen shape and its measured numbers
- [ ] New stack running on inari as at most one container or systemd service behind Apache; R2R, Hatchet, RabbitMQ, MinIO, Unstructured, graph_clustering, NPM and the monitor removed from compose and code
- [ ] Intake rewritten against the new store (harvest, prepare, download, embed, prune), with ticket 0011's completeness check
- [ ] Frontend calls the new endpoint; smoke tests and CI target the new stack (0006)
- [ ] Tickets made moot by the rebuild closed with a pointer here (0007 R2R ops parts, 0017, 0018, 0024 and others found during the work)
